# pr-hero's own exclusions, on top of the 9 shipped defaults (lockfiles, minified, snapshots).
# Dialect: a gitignore(5) subset, read from the BASE ref under CI. Last matching rule wins.
#
# Scope of this file: prose only. Research notes, benchmark ledgers and the roadmap are argued in
# review comments and PR descriptions, not by a hunter — and their diffs are large, so reviewing them
# spends real budget on text that cannot break at runtime.
#
# Deliberately NOT excluded: anything executable, or prose that CARRIES something executable.
# Two goldens in our own Martian corpus live exactly there — shell under `set -u` inside a markdown
# runbook, and a macOS-only `sed -i ''` in a shell script (docs/research/local-logic-misses.md).
# A blanket `docs/**` or `*.md` rule would make this reviewer blind to that class.

docs/research/**
docs/benchmarks/**
ROADMAP.md

# Re-include the machine-readable case lists that live under the excluded dirs: they are data the
# engine and its tests read, not prose, and a wrong line number there silently mis-scores a benchmark.
!docs/benchmarks/*.json
